{
  "_id": "fhSubVoltBeans01",
  "name": "Voltbeans",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Glossy yellow capsules pressed in someone's apartment kitchen and sold at warehouse parties. The hit lands fast and lasts about as long as the bassline. Quality varies by batch and by who owes who a favor that week.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks and a +2 bonus to Charisma (Performance) checks.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 12 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Voltbeans (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Voltbeans.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Constitution saving throws made to maintain concentration.</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 11 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 1 day, or half that if you succeed on a DC 12 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal you take a -2 penalty to all ability checks and saving throws and have disadvantage on initiative rolls. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 15% chance you overdose: you take 2d6 poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can slip a dose into food or drink within 5 feet. A creature that consumes it is dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to ingested substances, such as a Pill Cutter or a Tincture Dropper.</em></p>"
    },
